From 9abd7a982301ce70d1ad5f57ef7b122be08367e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:47:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): a card the Board shows held by a
 respawn guard never takes the worker pickup budget

worker-1 2026-11-12 11:40-11:57Z: four guarded hub cards (subscription_quota_reset,
active_pr) at priority 360..20801 sat at the top of the pickup order and filled the
3-card batch every tick (49 imports in 17 min), so six cards pinned to machine:worker-1
waited budget_exhausted while running < max_in_progress (t_01a1cf9fa5c6616f).

The dispatcher's respawn_guarded events travel with the card history, so the replica
shows the hold before this machine copies the card. _evaluate now reads that hold
(kanban_pickup_held.board_hold, read-only) and copies such a card outside the budget
(at most FREE_PER_TICK per tick): the local guard still decides on its own copy, and
eba518b16a keeps a copy it holds. A copy it does not hold is evicted and is not copied
again for RECHECK_SECONDS unless its Board hold changes, so it is not re-imported every
tick. A capped tick (note_capped) records a held pinned card as `hold`, keeping
budget_exhausted for cards a slot would start. An unreadable hold takes the budget as
before.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_pickup_held.py              |  64 ++++++++
 hermes_cli/kanban_worker_node.py              |  30 +++-
 .../test_kanban_pickup_held_budget.py         | 153 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 241 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 hermes_cli/kanban_pickup_held.py
